This test connects a socket ahead of the client socket and expects accept() to
return that connection first. Both connects are non-blocking and on illumos the
later one can be established first, in which case socketpair() returns a
pair but the test fails. Wait for the first connection to complete.

diff -wpruN --no-dereference '--exclude=*.orig' a~/Lib/test/test_socket.py a/Lib/test/test_socket.py
--- a~/Lib/test/test_socket.py	1970-01-01 00:00:00
+++ a/Lib/test/test_socket.py	1970-01-01 00:00:00
@@ -5429,6 +5429,9 @@ class PurePythonSocketPairTest(SocketPai
                     inject_sock.connect(sockname[:2])
                 except (BlockingIOError, InterruptedError):
                     pass
+                # Wait for this connection to be established, so that it is
+                # ahead of the client socket in the accept queue.
+                select.select([], [inject_sock], [], support.SHORT_TIMEOUT)
                 inject_sock.setblocking(True)
             return sockname
 
